findings.evidence:
`if this.src == 0 and (bar_index - this.createdBar < originBars or this.maxAway < awayATR)`: only chart arrays (src 0) are locked; HTF FVGs are src 2.
An HTF FVG is accepted with `hGap >= 0`, so it can be adjacent to price. It also gets:
- density +0.20;
- freshness about 1;
- often confluence 0.35 to 0.7, because a tall daily gap contains session opens or EQ levels inside [bottom - tol, top + tol].
On the draw side it scores about 9 (tapered proximity) + 10 + 7.5 + 16 + 24 = 66. That beats a normal 2-ATR pool (about 58) while price is touching its edge.

